; Colliding events whose boxes end up 2^31 or more rows apart. A vertical
; border of 1.4e9 makes an event's box taller than int can hold; libass
; converts the height out of int's range, undefined in C, which saturates
; when built with GCC for armv7 and keeps the low 32 bits when built with GCC
; for aarch64, whose vector conversion of the box takes that path. Moved up
; clear of the bottom line, the tall box and the one pushed above it start
; near INT_MIN, and cmp_rect_y0's int subtraction then wraps, so the order
; glibc's merge sort gives the boxes decides where the top-aligned events go.
